============================================================================================
5.3 TOKEN EFFICIENCY - BY STAGE
============================================================================================

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Sign convention of token_saving_vs_baseline_pct (worked example)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
token_saving_vs_baseline_pct = (json_baseline_indexing_tokens - format_indexing_tokens) / json_baseline_indexing_tokens * 100
  -> computed at the INDEXING stage only (it is null for json rows, the baseline itself).
  -> POSITIVE = format uses FEWER indexing tokens than JSON (a saving).
  -> NEGATIVE = format uses MORE indexing tokens than JSON (a cost).

  Worked example (bpolicy, fixed, 256):
    json indexing_tokens = 634,547  (baseline)
    toon indexing_tokens = 639,432  -> computed -0.77%  (column reports -0.77%)
    yaml indexing_tokens = 634,038  -> computed +0.08%  (column reports +0.08%)
    TOON is WORSE than JSON at indexing time; YAML is BETTER.

