[table saved -> thesis_tables\5_3_index_vs_prompt_pct_by_format.csv]

  Mechanism note: TOON's saving is BATCH-DEPENDENT - its header row is
  amortized over the k records serialized together, so its per-stage
  advantage shifts with how many chunks are grouped at that stage.
  YAML's saving is CONSTANT-RATE - lighter syntax with no header to
  amortize, so its advantage vs JSON is stable across both stages.

