============================================================================================
5.5 GENERATION FIDELITY
============================================================================================

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
faithfulness vs ragas_faithfulness: duplicate check
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Pearson r(faithfulness, ragas_faithfulness) = 0.7881
  Mean absolute difference                    = 0.0341
  faithfulness >= ragas_faithfulness in        70.8% of rows

  VERDICT: NOT a duplicate. r=0.75 indicates correlated but distinct
  constructs - `faithfulness` is the single frozen-judge fraction-of-
  claims-supported score used online during the run; ragas_faithfulness
  is the separate decompose-then-verify RAGAS protocol (Es et al. 2024),
  one of the four pre-registered triangulated fidelity metrics.
  `faithfulness` is therefore NOT part of the formal triangulation set
  and is excluded from all analysis below; ragas_faithfulness is used
  throughout as specified.

